  "body": "## Summary\n\nDependent on #353; base branch `codex/payment-notification-identity-20260914`.\nThis is a prerequisite safety repair for future missed-callback recovery, not\nthe recovery worker or a payment-provider activation.\n\n- Keep PlaceToPay/PayPhone query application inside the caller's transaction\n  using a local savepoint. Retain pre-existing caller locks; roll back all\n  payment/intent/ledger/receipt/audit effects if the caller later fails.\n- Revalidate the stored immutable binding and exact result identity, amount,\n  currency and certainty before applying financial state.\n- Keep the bounded production transport and original callback validation;\n  add an injectable query/clock boundary for contract tests. Record query\n  response observation time, not callback/start time.\n- Add 27 PostgreSQL reconciliation cases. Repair the test harness's missing\n  capture-ledger dependencies using the real existing sale/rental migrations\n  and a guarded disposable ORM-base fixture.\n- Document the threat model, source evidence, rollback, staging limitations\n  and the still-open durable-worker/shared-query-budget requirements.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Final database source `bb54a2232bad46344b58a4dd91103d84431fcb85`:\n  `sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh` \u2014 **72 examples, 0 failures**,\n  PostgreSQL 16, 30.8132 seconds. Synthetic contracts, not provider sandboxes.\n- Focused backend regression \u2014 **118 examples, 0 failures** (16.9829 seconds).\n  This overlaps the full backend suite and excludes optional DB cases.\n- Full backend on final source \u2014 **2,589 examples, 0 failures** (54.6890 seconds).\n- Provider-execution migration rollback/reapply regression \u2014 passed.\n- Final catalog audit \u2014 exit 0; no gate/scanner/catalog-decision changes.\n- `sh -n` and whitespace checks passed; new local doc links resolve.\n- Intermediate compile/fixture failures and restricted Docker attempts are\n  preserved in `docs/payments/reconciliation-atomicity-2026-09-14.md`.\n\n## Compatibility / migrations / rollback\n\nNo production migration/backfill, public API, generated client or web/mobile\nchange. Original references and financial history remain intact. Only the\ndisposable DB harness gains schema dependencies; no financial trigger is\nstubbed or disabled. No screenshots were produced (no UI changes).\n\nCode rollback requires disabling any dependent recovery caller first; the prior\ncode restores the caller-transaction composition defect. Preserve all evidence;\ndo not delete ledger, receipt, operation or inbox history.\n\n## Risks / configuration / blocked verification\n\nNo live charge, sandbox transaction, staging deployment or production action.\nExisting staging health is reachable, but all six hosting inspections reported\n`hosting_authentication_unavailable` at 2026-09-15T03:15:13.311Z; provider\nqualification is false and deployed SHA unknown. Restore authorized app-scoped\nFly access and obtain/qualify provider sandbox accounts before activation.\n\nNo new worker/flag is enabled. Missing callbacks, distributed query budgets,\nlease fencing, unknown-resource creates, late-paid/expired fulfillment and the\nremaining settlement/recurring/payout work are still open. Official PayPhone\ndocs also identify a separate canceled-as-declined mapping requiring a\nhistory-preserving follow-up; this patch does not silently reinterpret it.\n\n## Review order\n\n#331 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #340 \u2192 #343 \u2192 #347 \u2192 #350 \u2192 #353 \u2192 this PR.\nStaging #344 remains independent after #343. Do not merge or deploy to production.\n\nSee ADR 0119 and the dated verification report for exact commands, commits,\nobserved timestamps, source URLs, evidence limits and next implementation gates.\n",
